      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'll just copy and paste my comment from another canny that was basically saying the same thing about the gesture system.\n\nGestures feel impossible to even do accurately now because of this system. Whenever I have the gesture mode activated it instantly starts doing gestures just because my hands are normally resting on the controller and I never have any idea what gesture I'm doing.\n\nTo make matters worse, the gesture you have on when you toggle the gesture system gets stuck when you turn it off, so I literally have to pull my camera out or run to a mirror every time I turn it on/off to make sure I'm not stuck on a gesture.\n\nThe old way (before this patch) was that you'd squeeze the controller in to do the gestures. This was a bit harder to do but at least I had a better way of knowing what gesture I'm doing. Before that, there was the system which allowed you to use gestures with your touchpad. Why none of these two things are even offered as options now I don't know. Why are we forced to conform to this one specific way of using gestures instead of given an option?\n\nIf this is really the system VRChat is now sticking with and is happy with, which IMO is a step back from the previous patch with squeezing for gestures, at the bare minimum we need some kind of HUD indicator. We need something that tells us which gesture we're using because I literally don't even use my gestures anymore because I have no way of knowing if I'm doing them unless I'm staring at myself in a mirror or camera. I'm able to tell exactly what gesture I'm using when holding a vive controller or a rift controller, with the index controllers I am absolutely clueless because of this implementation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
